{"agent_id":"pp3g-TSZN-read-only-plan-review-do-not-modify-files-do-not-2da6","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T00:55:03.465121198Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","comment_uuid":"cad0888a-ece3-4cc0-941b-85e3e0d9cfb2","author":"pp3g-TSZN-read-only-plan-review-do-not-modify-files-do-not-2da6","content":"## [VERDICT] READ-ONLY PLAN REVIEW — FOLLOW-UP PLAN (P3-r3) on #125 — 2026-08-08\n\nScope: plan-review only. No files modified, no commit, no push. #125 NOT closed. Every plan-item citation re-derived from fork@7c5b3e88 (clean tree, HEAD 7c5b3e88).\n\n== HEADLINE ==\n\nCHANGES-REQUIRED (narrow). COVERAGE: PASS — the 4 items cover ALL of the audit's recommended follow-ups (00:36 verdict). EVIDENCE DISCIPLINE: PASS for the assertions (items 1/3/4 fully grounded; item 2's assertion grounded) — but 3 items carry implementation assumptions that, if implemented literally, either cannot be tested (item 2), reintroduce a fail-open (item 1), or break the repair path (item 4). These are precision amendments to the same 4 items, not scope changes; keep all 4.\n\n== CHECK 1 — COVERAGE vs audit verdict 2026-08-08 00:36 ==\n\n| Audit recommendation | Plan item | Covered? |\n|---|---|---|\n| RECOMMENDED (a) remote-enumeration hardening (SHOULD-CONSIDER #1) | 1 | YES |\n| RECOMMENDED (b) regression test warn-and-continue (NIT #3 part 1) | 2 | YES |\n| RECOMMENDED (b) regression test marker-write-on-skip (NIT #3 part 2) | 3 | YES |\n| RECOMMENDED (c) integrity repair clear-order (NIT #4) | 4 | YES |\n| NIT #2 G6 'missing issues dir' durability | — | Not covered; audit explicitly calls it HARMLESS and attaches no recommendation — acceptable as conscious scope-out, but the plan should SAY so (see G4) |\n\nAll three RECOMMENDED FOLLOW-UPS and both actionable NITs are mapped 1:1. No other recommendation exists in the 00:36 verdict (PART C/BOTTOM LINE add none). COVERAGE: PASS.\n\n== CHECK 2 — EVIDENCE DISCIPLINE (each item re-derived from fork@7c5b3e88) ==\n\n| Item | Cited mechanism | Re-derivation | Grounded? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 remote-enumeration | audit SC#1: v2_file_path_decision fail-opens when tracker_remote names nonexistent remote while others exist; 'list_git_remotes exists' | CONFIRMED: hub_v3.rs:836-840 — if !remote_configured(repo_dir, remote) -> Allowed; remote_configured (hub_v3.rs:859-867) = 'git remote get-url <named>' success only — never enumerates other remotes. list_git_remotes EXISTS (sync/mod.rs:118-137) but is PRIVATE and returns empty vec on ANY failure ('soft signal, not a hard error', sync/mod.rs:112-116) | Grounded assertion; UNGROUNDED implementation path — see R1 |\n| 2 warn-and-continue regression test | audit NIT #3 + audit finding 4 (7c5b3e88 is real post-commit fix: 5ada263a had ? on dispatcher) | CONFIRMED: daemon.rs:281-325; 7c5b3e88 diff removes the ? (Ok(...) match at 288-306, outer Err arm warns at 322-324, loop continues). BUT daemon.rs has NO #[cfg(test)] module and NO tracing-capture test infra exists anywhere in the crate (tracing-subscriber is a dep, Cargo.toml:53, but no subscriber harness; no tracing-test). The tick hydrate step is embedded ~40 lines deep inside two nested loops + HEARTBEAT_EVERY_N gate (daemon.rs:166-325) | Grounded assertion (that warn-and-continue is the behavior); UNGROUNDED implementation path — 'add test asserting the tick loop continues + warns' is not implementable against the embedded loop — see R2 |\n| 3 marker-write-on-skip test | audit NIT #3 (G3 confirmed live organically) | CONFIRMED: hydration.rs:1370-1374 writes marker_path on the Forbidden skip arm; fixture setup_remote_v3_local_v2_only EXISTS and is already used by test_maybe_auto_hydrate_remote_only_v3_markers_skips (hydration.rs:2715-2752) — the new test reuses it and asserts LAST_HYDRATED_REF_FILE (.last-hydrated-ref, hydration.rs:1282) | FULLY GROUNDED — directly implementable |\n| 4 integrity clear-order | audit NIT #4 ('consider') | CONFIRMED: integrity_cmd.rs:405 db.clear_shared_data() runs BEFORE the dispatcher's locked re-check at 406 (hydrate_v2_safely). A flip between the unlocked pre-check (353) and the locked re-check leaves empty-but-recoverable DB. BUT: acquire_hub_lock (sync/cache.rs:56-60) is NON-REENTRANT — file-based create_new + 30s timeout; if integrity_cmd holds the lock and then calls hydrate_v2_safely, the dispatcher re-acquires -> 30s wait -> Err -> Skipped -> repair reports Fail EVERY time, not only on flip | Grounded assertion; UNGROUNDED implementation path — see R3 |\n\nNo item depends on builder self-report. The disproved 'all 3 FAIL' claim is nowhere in P3-r3.\n\n== CHECK 3 — GAPS ==\n\nR1 (MUST ADD, item 1): list_git_remotes returns empty on git failure — 'Allowed only on zero remotes' implemented literally would treat enumeration FAILURE as zero remotes -> Allowed -> fail-open, the exact class #125 exists to close. Spec: enumeration must distinguish empty-success from empty-failure (Result-returning or exit-status check); Allowed ONLY on a confirmed successful enumeration of zero remotes. Also: list_git_remotes is private in sync/mod.rs — needs pub(crate) or a local equivalent. Keep the existing test v2_file_path_decision_v2_only_no_remote_allowed (hub_v3.rs:4702-4710) green — it already pins the zero-remotes case (passes remote='origin', no remotes -> Allowed); no conflict with the existing 8 decision tests.\n\nR2 (MUST ADD, item 2): spec the testability refactor — extract the tick hydrate step (daemon.rs:281-325) into a standalone function (e.g., fn tick_hydrate(...) -> Result<Option<HydrationStats>> implementing the v3/v2 branches + warn handling) and assert: dispatcher Err is consumed (caller match warns, does NOT propagate; the loop continues), and the v2-Skipped arm warns. 'Asserts warns' needs either the extraction returning an outcome enum or a tracing subscriber harness (no existing infra). Without the refactor this item cannot be implemented as a unit test.\n\nR3 (MUST ADD, item 4): spec the lock sharing — the locked re-check, clear_shared_data, and hydrate must run under ONE lock acquisition (e.g., dispatcher variant that accepts an already-held HubWriteLock, or a locked clear+hydrate helper in integrity_cmd). If the Builder just moves the decision earlier and calls hydrate_v2_safely afterward, the non-reentrant lock (sync/cache.rs:56) makes the repair fail 100% of the time (30s wait -> Err -> Skipped -> CheckStatus::Fail). Also: re-emit (integrity_cmd.rs:379) stays before the clear — safe either way, but the plan should note the ordering is re-emit -> locked re-check -> clear -> hydrate.\n\nG4 (SHOULD CONSIDER, item on scope): NIT #2 (G6 'missing issues dir' durability) is consciously excluded — the audit calls it harmless (read_all_issue_files empty for both missing and empty; hydrate early-returns) and r2's gate supersedes the interim control. The plan should record this as a deliberate scope decision so a later reader can't mistake it for an omission.\n\nG5 (SHOULD CONSIDER, availability note): with item 1, tracker_remote=ghost + real v2-ONLY origin -> Forbidden (conservative; audit's chosen design). Legitimate v2-only remotes (tracker_remote valid) are unaffected (existing test remote_v2_only_allowed, hub_v3.rs:4743-4763). Optionally probe enumerated remotes instead of blanket-Forbid — out of audit scope, note only.\n\nG6 (NIT): docs — plan's 'fork code + tests only' is defensible (r2 already downgraded the RESOLVED claims); a one-line crosslink-fork.md note on the r3 gate behavior is optional.\n\n== BOTTOM LINE ==\n\nPLAN VERDICT: CHANGES-REQUIRED (narrow; #125 stays OPEN). Coverage complete, evidence discipline clean on assertions, ordering sound. Before dispatch, fold in R1 (enumeration must fail closed on enumeration failure + visibility), R2 (daemon tick-hydrate extraction + warn observation strategy), R3 (single-lock design for the integrity repair), and record G4 as a deliberate scope decision. Items 3 is fully implementable as written. #125 NOT closed.","created_at":"2026-08-08T00:55:03.455947957Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:OzSIJAjWegmzApqHxCSQIwR1XIs1N/rnhxmHD5zQTCE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgKJLC1CaP0l6a1Il1ESmpqJjajXo87meHpsG867gfUhIAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAyCBDm98QbYyDcPa88TfLa7sLv/p0A4jPcgGhD2/JtAYnawtZkaGHq/V+6+gDjtwkQ2/19FdFcSFdMSK/yaz4Dw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:OzSIJAjWegmzApqHxCSQIwR1XIs1N/rnhxmHD5zQTCE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgKJLC1CaP0l6a1Il1ESmpqJjajXo87meHpsG867gfUhIAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPmAKGWzOjiFfxSyH5ChFCjSJvYH2Wf9kBIuJr706PQ5bZxcZ6ay1Ygb9by0GeX5z9ZcNmQ4jLe7s/CGMW+s8gc="}
